# Arm: fable — Claude Fable 5, direct Anthropic key on the OpenAI-compat surface.
# Paste into this Mac's credentials.env (replaces the model block and the
# Inkbox identity block).
# VERIFIED 2026-08-06 against Anthropic's first-party docs: model id
# claude-fable-5 with a 1M-token context window (default, no beta header) and
# 128K max output (platform.claude.com → models/overview + context-windows);
# OpenAI-compat surface at https://api.anthropic.com/v1/ with Bearer auth,
# streaming + tools supported (→ libraries/openai-sdk). Compat-layer caveats:
# no prompt caching / extended thinking; max_tokens is REQUIRED on every
# request (the interception proxy injects it when the client omits it).
FB_ARM="fable"
MODEL_ID="claude-fable-5"
MODEL_UPSTREAM_URL="https://api.anthropic.com/v1"
MODEL_API_KEY=""   # ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
MODEL_NPM="@ai-sdk/openai-compatible"
# MODEL_CONTEXT/MODEL_OUTPUT intentionally unset → OpenCode defaults (fleet
# policy: only muse pins limits). Documented caps for reference: 1,000,000
# ctx / 128,000 out.

# ── Inkbox identity (PER-AGENT — this Mac's agent, never shared) ──────────────
# Same three fields as the Inkbox section of credentials.env.example, kept in
# every arm file so one paste provisions the whole per-machine block. Use an
# identity-scoped key (stage 60 asserts exactly 1 identity is visible).
INKBOX_API_KEY=""
INKBOX_VAULT_KEY=""     # client-side vault decryption key — Inkbox cannot recover it
INKBOX_AGENT_HANDLE=""  # e.g. "founderbench-fable"
